  "texts": {
    "preamble": "The State Of M.P. vs Ramesh Sahu on 6 January, 2026 Author: Avanindra Kumar Singh Bench: Avanindra Kumar Singh Neutral Citation No. 2026:Mphc-Jbp:607 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Jabalpur Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice Avanindra Kumar Singh On The 6 th Of January, 2026 Criminal Appeal No. 418 of 2002 The State Of M.P. Versus Ramesh Sahu Appearance: Shri Pankaj Raj - Panel Lawyer for the appellant/State. None for the respondent.",
    "facts": "Now a PUD received from Special Judge (SC/ST) Act, District Panna informing that respondent/accused is not appearing before the Court from 15/06/2020. This appeal is filed being aggrieved of the judgment dated 20/01/2001 passed by the Additional Sessions Judge, Panna in Criminal Appeal No.37/2000, whereby acquitting the respondent from the charges punishable under Section 16(1)(a)(1) of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act. The appeal is filed on the following grounds:- (i) that the Court below failed to see that the respondent is a shop keeper/kirana merchant. NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2026:MPHC-JBP:607 2 CRA-418-2002 The State Of M.P. vs Ramesh Sahu on 6 January, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/70894695/ 1 (ii) that the Court below has not appreciated the material available on record in it true perspective. The sampled salt was send for analysis and, thereafter, the report of Public Analysis was received that it was adulterated. Hence, charge-sheet was filed against him. As mentioned in Para-11 of the judgment when the Public Analysis report was received on 21/05/1996, the complaint was filed on 27/01/1997 i.e. after the period of one year and there was no explanation was given.",
    "arguments": "",
